<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ treasurer &quot;official&quot; one day ahead of budget.</title>
<headline>NZ treasurer &quot;official&quot; one day ahead of budget.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New Zealand Parliament on Wednesday formally established the post of treasurer only a day before Treasurer Winston Peters was due to deliver his first budget.</p>
<p>The treasurer's job, the senior of three finance ministers, was established in December specifically for Peters at the time his nationalist New Zealand First Party and the conservative National Party struck a coalition deal outlining their programme for the next three years.</p>
</text>
